menu "Wi-Fi CMSIS-DAP Transport"

config WIFI_DAP_USB_WAIT_MS
    int "USB host detection window before starting the SoftAP (ms)"
    default 3000
    range 0 60000
    help
        At boot the probe waits up to this long for a USB host to attach and
        enumerate the HID interface. If a host shows up inside the window the
        SoftAP is NEVER started and the probe stays in USB mode, because
        Wi-Fi RF activity on ESP32-S3 corrupts USB OTG HID transfers.
        Only when no host ever appears does the probe fall back to the
        wireless transport (SoftAP + TCP 50000).
        Raise this value if your host enumerates slowly; set 0 to skip the
        wait and start Wi-Fi immediately.

endmenu
